1
00:00:06,799 --> 00:00:08,592
Monica:
COME IN.

2
00:00:08,634 --> 00:00:11,470
I'VE BEEN
WAITING FOR YOU.

3
00:00:13,806 --> 00:00:15,098
HI, I JUST...

4
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:16,433
( screams )

5
00:00:16,475 --> 00:00:17,768
MY GOD!

6
00:00:17,810 --> 00:00:19,102
OH, MY GOD, MONICA!

7
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:20,437
OH, MY GOD.

8
00:00:20,479 --> 00:00:21,772
I'M SORRY. SORRY.

9
00:00:21,814 --> 00:00:23,106
I-I WAS, UM...

10
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:24,525
I WAS TAKING A NAP.

11
00:00:24,566 --> 00:00:27,486
SINCE WHEN DO YOU TAKE NAPS
IN THAT POSITION?

12
00:00:29,488 --> 00:00:31,406
GOD, MONICA, SAY YOU WERE
WAITING FOR A GUY.

13
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:33,074
PLEASE SAY YOU WERE
WAITING FOR A GUY.

14
00:00:33,116 --> 00:00:34,451
YES. YES, I WAS.

15
00:00:34,493 --> 00:00:35,786
A GUY.

16
00:00:35,828 --> 00:00:37,621
FROM WORK.

17
00:00:37,663 --> 00:00:39,623
I'M SEEING A GUY FROM WORK!

18
00:00:39,665 --> 00:00:41,000
HA!

19
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:43,794
OH, THAT CUTE WAITER GUY
FROM YOUR RESTAURANT.

20
00:00:43,836 --> 00:00:47,046
THE ONE THAT LOOKS LIKE
A NONTHREATENING RAY LIOTTA?

21
00:00:47,088 --> 00:00:48,632
UH-HUH! THAT ONE.

22
00:00:48,674 --> 00:00:50,049
YOU KNOW WHAT?

23
00:00:50,091 --> 00:00:52,302
JUST GIVE ME A SECOND,
I'LL BE OUT OF YOUR HAIR.

24
00:00:52,344 --> 00:00:53,929
I'M JUST GOING TO GRAB A JACKET.

25
00:00:53,971 --> 00:00:58,058
WHEN I GET BACK,
I WANT EVERY LITTLE DETAIL.

26
00:00:59,351 --> 00:01:00,811
( knocking )

27
00:01:00,853 --> 00:01:02,145
MAYBE THAT'S HIM.

28
00:01:02,187 --> 00:01:03,271
OKAY, UM...

29
00:01:03,313 --> 00:01:05,357
OKAY, UM...

30
00:01:06,692 --> 00:01:09,236
IT'S JUST JOEY AND ROSS.

31
00:01:09,277 --> 00:01:10,821
WHY AREN'T YOU GUYS
AT THE MOVIE?

32
00:01:10,863 --> 00:01:13,073
WE WERE, BUT ROSS WAS
TALKING SO LOUD ON HIS PHONE

33
00:01:13,114 --> 00:01:14,449
THEY THREW US OUT.

34
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:18,037
I HAD TO TALK LOUD
BECAUSE THE MOVIE WAS LOUD.

35
00:01:19,287 --> 00:01:20,581
HE'S TALKING TO LONDON.

36
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:21,916
OH, MY GOD!

37
00:01:21,957 --> 00:01:23,417
DID HE GET IN
TOUCH WITH EMILY?

38
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:24,835
WELL, NO. NOT YET.

39
00:01:24,877 --> 00:01:26,628
HE'S CALLING EVERYONE
ON HER SIDE OF THE FAMILY

40
00:01:26,670 --> 00:01:29,088
HOPING THAT SOMEONE WILL
HELP HIM GET IN TOUCH WITH HER.

41
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:32,426
I DON'T CARE IF I SAID
SOME OTHER GIRL'S NAME

42
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:34,386
YOU PRISSY OLD TWIT!

43
00:01:34,428 --> 00:01:35,930
HEY, ROSS.

44
00:01:35,971 --> 00:01:38,682
WAY TO SUCK UP
TO THE FAMILY.

45
00:01:38,724 --> 00:01:40,267
( chuckling )

46
00:01:40,308 --> 00:01:42,269
AH... AH...

47
00:01:45,064 --> 00:01:47,524
I'M SO GLAD
YOU GUYS ARE ALL HERE.

48
00:01:47,566 --> 00:01:50,903
MY OFFICE FINALLY GOT
WRINKLE-FREE FAX PAPER!

49
00:01:58,285 --> 00:02:03,331
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

50
00:02:03,373 --> 00:02:05,709
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

51
00:02:05,751 --> 00:02:08,545
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

52
00:02:08,587 --> 00:02:13,050
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

53
00:02:13,092 --> 00:02:15,010
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

54
00:02:15,052 --> 00:02:18,055
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

55
00:02:18,097 --> 00:02:21,683
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

56
00:02:21,725 --> 00:02:23,769
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

57
00:02:23,811 --> 00:02:26,396
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

58
00:02:26,438 --> 00:02:28,607
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

59
00:02:28,649 --> 00:02:31,819
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

60
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:37,449
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

61
00:02:40,619 --> 00:02:42,704
NO, NO, NO.
HEY.

62
00:02:42,746 --> 00:02:45,666
VOMIT TUX.
NO, NO. VOMIT TUX.

63
00:02:45,707 --> 00:02:47,793
DON'T WORRY.
I HAD IT DRY-CLEANED.

64
00:02:47,835 --> 00:02:49,128
VOMIT TUX?

65
00:02:49,168 --> 00:02:50,796
WHO VOMITED ON...

66
00:02:50,838 --> 00:02:52,339
YOU KNOW WHAT?

67
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:54,842
WHAT YOU UP TO, JOE?

68
00:02:54,883 --> 00:02:58,012
WELL, THEY'RE DOING
THIS TELETHON THING ON TV

69
00:02:58,053 --> 00:03:00,514
AND MY AGENT
GOT ME A JOB AS COHOST.

70
00:03:00,555 --> 00:03:02,223
OH, THAT'S GREAT!

71
00:03:02,265 --> 00:03:06,645
A LITTLE GOOD DEED FOR PBS,
PLUS SOME TV EXPOSURE.

72
00:03:06,687 --> 00:03:10,732
NOW, THAT'S THE KIND OF MATH
JOEY LIKES TO DO.

73
00:03:10,774 --> 00:03:13,068
YUCK! PBS.

74
00:03:13,110 --> 00:03:14,361
WHAT'S WRONG WITH PBS?

75
00:03:14,402 --> 00:03:16,071
WHAT'S RIGHT WITH THEM?

76
00:03:17,489 --> 00:03:19,366
WHY DON'T YOU LIKE PBS, PHEEBS?

77
00:03:19,407 --> 00:03:21,785
OKAY, 'CAUSE RIGHT AFTER
MY MOM KILLED HERSELF

78
00:03:21,827 --> 00:03:24,913
I WAS JUST IN THIS REALLY BAD
PLACE, YOU KNOW, PERSONALLY.

79
00:03:27,041 --> 00:03:29,543
I JUST THOUGHT THAT
IT WOULD MAKE ME FEEL BETTER

80
00:03:29,584 --> 00:03:31,045
IF I WROTE TO SESAME STREET

81
00:03:31,086 --> 00:03:33,547
'CAUSE THEY WERE SO NICE
WHEN I WAS A LITTLE KID.

82
00:03:33,588 --> 00:03:35,132
NO ONE EVER WROTE BACK.

83
00:03:35,174 --> 00:03:38,301
WELL, YOU KNOW A LOT OF THOSE
MUPPETS DON'T HAVE THUMBS.

84
00:03:38,343 --> 00:03:41,013
ALL I GOT WAS A LOUSY KEY CHAIN

85
00:03:41,055 --> 00:03:44,349
AND BY THAT TIME,
I WAS LIVING IN A BOX.

86
00:03:44,391 --> 00:03:46,143
I DIDN'T HAVE KEYS.

87
00:03:46,185 --> 00:03:47,186
I'M SORRY, PHEEBS.

88
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:48,436
I JUST, YOU KNOW

89
00:03:48,478 --> 00:03:50,480
I JUST WANTED TO DO
A GOOD DEED LIKE...

90
00:03:50,522 --> 00:03:52,066
LIKE YOU DID
WITH THE BABIES.

91
00:03:52,107 --> 00:03:53,441
THIS ISN'T A GOOD DEED.

92
00:03:53,483 --> 00:03:55,069
YOU JUST WANT TO GET ON TV.

93
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:56,570
THIS IS TOTALLY SELFISH.

94
00:03:56,611 --> 00:03:58,113
WHOA, WHOA, WHOA!

95
00:03:58,155 --> 00:04:01,116
WHAT ABOUT YOU HAVING
THOSE BABIES FOR YOUR BROTHER?

96
00:04:01,158 --> 00:04:02,617
TALK ABOUT SELFISH.

97
00:04:02,659 --> 00:04:06,329
WHAT... WHAT ARE
YOU TALKING ABOUT?

98
00:04:06,371 --> 00:04:07,873
IT WAS A REALLY
NICE THING AND ALL

99
00:04:07,915 --> 00:04:09,750
BUT IT MADE YOU FEEL
REALLY GOOD, RIGHT?

100
00:04:09,791 --> 00:04:11,292
YEAH. SO?

101
00:04:11,334 --> 00:04:14,755
WELL, IT MADE YOU FEEL GOOD,
SO THAT MAKES IT SELFISH.

102
00:04:14,796 --> 00:04:17,758
LOOK, THERE'S NO UNSELFISH
GOOD DEEDS. SORRY.

103
00:04:17,799 --> 00:04:19,134
YES, THERE ARE.

104
00:04:19,176 --> 00:04:21,720
THERE ARE TOTALLY GOOD DEEDS
THAT ARE SELFLESS.

105
00:04:21,762 --> 00:04:23,764
WELL, MAY I ASK
FOR ONE EXAMPLE?

106
00:04:23,805 --> 00:04:26,808
YEAH, IT'S...
YOU KNOW... THERE'S...

107
00:04:26,850 --> 00:04:28,810
NO, YOU MAY NOT.

108
00:04:28,852 --> 00:04:32,773
THAT'S BECAUSE
ALL PEOPLE ARE SELFISH.

109
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:35,609
ARE YOU CALLING
ME SELFISH?

110
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:38,403
ARE YOU CALLING
YOU PEOPLE?

111
00:04:38,445 --> 00:04:39,613
YEAH. WELL...

112
00:04:39,654 --> 00:04:41,698
SORRY TO BURST
THAT BUBBLE, PHEEBS

113
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:44,284
BUT SELFLESS GOOD DEEDS
DON'T EXIST, OKAY?

114
00:04:44,325 --> 00:04:46,995
AND YOU KNOW THE DEAL
ON SANTA CLAUS, RIGHT?

115
00:04:47,037 --> 00:04:50,165
I'M GOING TO FIND
A SELFLESS GOOD DEED.

116
00:04:50,207 --> 00:04:53,334
I'M GOING TO BEAT YOU,
YOU EVIL GENIUS.

117
00:04:53,376 --> 00:04:54,795
( phone rings )

118
00:04:54,836 --> 00:04:56,546
HELLO?

119
00:04:56,588 --> 00:04:58,048
HELLO, ROSS?

120
00:04:58,090 --> 00:05:00,134
EMILY? EM...
OH, MY GOD!

121
00:05:00,175 --> 00:05:01,468
OH, MY GOD, IT'S EMILY!

122
00:05:01,509 --> 00:05:02,803
IT'S EMILY, EVERYONE!

123
00:05:02,844 --> 00:05:04,179
SHH! SHH!

124
00:05:06,389 --> 00:05:07,474
HI.

125
00:05:07,515 --> 00:05:08,850
ROSS, I'M ONLY RINGING

126
00:05:08,892 --> 00:05:11,394
TO SAY STOP HARASSING
MY RELATIVES. GOOD-BYE.

127
00:05:11,436 --> 00:05:12,980
NO. WAIT, WAIT.
LOOK. OKAY, OKAY.

128
00:05:13,021 --> 00:05:15,274
YOU CAN HANG UP,
BUT I'M GOING TO KEEP CALLING.

129
00:05:15,315 --> 00:05:17,025
I'M GOING TO CALL
EVERYONE IN ENGLAND

130
00:05:17,067 --> 00:05:19,444
IF THAT'S WHAT IT TAKES
TO GET YOU TO TALK TO ME.

131
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:21,320
REALLY? ABOUT WHAT?

132
00:05:21,362 --> 00:05:22,656
LOOK, YOU'RE MY WIFE.

133
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:24,825
WE'RE...
WE'RE MARRIED, YOU KNOW.

134
00:05:24,866 --> 00:05:26,160
I... I LOVE YOU. I...

135
00:05:26,201 --> 00:05:27,869
I really miss you.

136
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:31,498
I MISS YOU, TOO.

137
00:05:31,539 --> 00:05:33,917
Well, at least I think I do.

138
00:05:33,959 --> 00:05:35,502
SHE'S TALKING.

139
00:05:35,543 --> 00:05:37,545
All ( whispering ):
YEA!

140
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:41,508
HEY, JOEY, WHEN

141
00:05:41,549 --> 00:05:44,427
YOU SAID THE DEAL
WITH SANTA CLAUS,
YOU MEANT...

142
00:05:44,469 --> 00:05:46,013
THAT HE DOESN'T EXIST.

143
00:05:46,054 --> 00:05:47,555
RIGHT.

144
00:05:52,144 --> 00:05:53,812
SO, CHANDLER,
HAVE YOU HEARD

145
00:05:53,854 --> 00:05:55,772
ABOUT MONICA'S
SECRET BOYFRIEND?

146
00:05:55,814 --> 00:05:57,232
UH... YEAH. SHE, UH...

147
00:05:57,274 --> 00:05:59,901
SHE, UH... SHE MIGHT
HAVE MENTIONED HIM. YEAH.

148
00:05:59,943 --> 00:06:01,444
SO, MON

149
00:06:01,486 --> 00:06:04,948
WHEN ARE WE GOING TO MEET
THIS NEW SECRET WAITER MAN?

150
00:06:04,990 --> 00:06:06,325
OH, HE'S REALLY SHY.

151
00:06:06,365 --> 00:06:08,367
I DON'T THINK HE'S
UP TO MEETING EVERYONE YET.

152
00:06:08,409 --> 00:06:11,330
YEAH, I DON'T THINK
HE'S UP TO MEETING EVERYONE YET.

153
00:06:11,370 --> 00:06:12,914
I DON'T CARE.

154
00:06:12,956 --> 00:06:15,542
I WANT TO MEET THIS GUY
WHO'S THE BEST SEX SHE EVER HAD.

155
00:06:15,583 --> 00:06:17,669
REALLY?

156
00:06:19,338 --> 00:06:20,881
THAT'S WHAT
YOU HEARD?

157
00:06:20,922 --> 00:06:22,465
YOU SAID THAT?

158
00:06:22,507 --> 00:06:24,134
I MIGHT HAVE SAID THAT.

159
00:06:24,176 --> 00:06:27,054
( laughing )

160
00:06:27,095 --> 00:06:28,763
WHY IS THAT FUNNY?

161
00:06:28,805 --> 00:06:30,224
BECAUSE I'M VERY

162
00:06:30,265 --> 00:06:32,433
HAPPY FOR HIM.

163
00:06:32,475 --> 00:06:35,270
AND YOU, YOU LUCKY DOG.

164
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:37,939
HI.

165
00:06:37,981 --> 00:06:39,398
HEY.
HI.

166
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:41,735
WELL, EMILY'S WILLING
TO WORK ON THE RELATIONSHIP.

167
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:43,195
THAT'S GREAT!

168
00:06:43,237 --> 00:06:44,403
IN LONDON.

169
00:06:44,445 --> 00:06:45,572
WHAT?

170
00:06:45,613 --> 00:06:47,490
SHE WANTS ME TO MOVE TO LONDON.

171
00:06:47,532 --> 00:06:48,742
BUT YOU LIVE HERE.

172
00:06:51,953 --> 00:06:54,164
YOU KNOW THAT.

173
00:06:54,206 --> 00:06:56,750
WHAT... WHAT...
WHAT ARE YOU
GOING TO DO?

174
00:06:56,791 --> 00:06:59,711
I BET IF I TALKED
TO CAROL AND SUSAN

175
00:06:59,753 --> 00:07:03,757
I COULD CONVINCE THEM
TO MOVE TO LONDON WITH BEN.

176
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:06,134
YEAH. I'M SURE YOUR EX-WIFE
WOULD BE MORE THAN HAPPY

177
00:07:06,176 --> 00:07:07,677
TO MOVE TO ANOTHER COUNTRY

178
00:07:07,719 --> 00:07:09,763
SO YOU CAN PATCH THINGS UP
WITH YOUR NEW WIFE.

179
00:07:11,639 --> 00:07:13,641
IT COULD HAPPEN.

180
00:07:18,563 --> 00:07:19,856
HOW YOU DOING?

181
00:07:19,898 --> 00:07:21,191
WELCOME.

182
00:07:21,233 --> 00:07:22,776
GOOD TO SEE YOU.

183
00:07:22,817 --> 00:07:24,443
THIS WILL BE YOUR PHONE.

184
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:29,699
THAT'S GREAT,
BUT, UH...

185
00:07:29,741 --> 00:07:32,869
I'M NOT REALLY EXPECTING
A LOT OF CALLS.

186
00:07:32,911 --> 00:07:35,538
NO, YOU ANSWER IT
AND TAKE PLEDGES.

187
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:36,957
BUT I'M THE HOST.

188
00:07:36,998 --> 00:07:39,334
NO, GARY COLLINS
IS THE HOST.

189
00:07:39,376 --> 00:07:41,711
YOU'LL BE
ANSWERING
THE PHONE.

190
00:07:41,753 --> 00:07:44,089
YOU DON'T SEEM
TO UNDERSTAND.

191
00:07:44,131 --> 00:07:46,465
SEE, I WAS
DR. DRAKE RAMORAY.

192
00:07:46,507 --> 00:07:49,177
WELL, HERE'S YOUR
PHONE, DOCTOR.

193
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:53,223
I CANNOT BELIEVE
I CAN'T FIND

194
00:07:53,265 --> 00:07:54,349
A SELFLESS
GOOD DEED.

195
00:07:54,391 --> 00:07:55,850
YOU KNOW THAT
REALLY OLD GUY

196
00:07:55,892 --> 00:07:57,352
THAT LIVES
NEXT DOOR TO ME?

197
00:07:57,394 --> 00:08:00,647
WELL, I SNUCK OVER THERE
AND RAKED UP ALL THE LEAVES

198
00:08:00,688 --> 00:08:02,983
ON HIS FRONT STOOP,
BUT HE CAUGHT ME

199
00:08:03,024 --> 00:08:05,277
AND FORCE-FED ME
CIDER AND COOKIES.

200
00:08:06,945 --> 00:08:09,030
THEN I FELT WONDERFUL.

201
00:08:09,072 --> 00:08:10,698
THAT OLD JACKASS.

202
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:12,491
YOU KNOW, MAYBE JOEY'S RIGHT.

203
00:08:12,533 --> 00:08:14,535
MAYBE ALL GOOD DEEDS
ARE SELFISH.

204
00:08:14,577 --> 00:08:16,455
I WILL FIND
A SELFLESS GOOD DEED

205
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:19,040
BECAUSE I JUST GAVE BIRTH
TO THREE CHILDREN

206
00:08:19,082 --> 00:08:21,001
AND I WILL NOT LET THEM
BE RAISED

207
00:08:21,042 --> 00:08:22,961
IN A WORLD WHERE JOEY IS RIGHT.

208
00:08:23,003 --> 00:08:24,212
HEY, MONICA?

209
00:08:24,254 --> 00:08:26,089
CAN I ASK YOU
A COOKING QUESTION?

210
00:08:26,131 --> 00:08:27,424
SURE.

211
00:08:27,466 --> 00:08:29,259
IF YOU'RE COOKING ON THE STOVE

212
00:08:29,301 --> 00:08:31,845
DOES THAT MEAN
THAT YOUR NEW
SECRET BOYFRIEND

213
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:33,680
IS BETTER IN BED
THAN RICHARD?

214
00:08:35,223 --> 00:08:36,557
CHANDLER!

215
00:08:37,892 --> 00:08:39,644
IS HE?

216
00:08:40,854 --> 00:08:42,063
LOOK, YOU KNOW WHAT?

217
00:08:42,105 --> 00:08:43,940
I THINK
I'M GOING TO RESPECT THE PRIVACY

218
00:08:43,982 --> 00:08:45,400
OF MY NEW SECRET BOYFRIEND.

219
00:08:45,442 --> 00:08:47,235
WHY?

220
00:08:49,237 --> 00:08:50,822
I MEAN IF THIS GUY WAS ME

221
00:08:50,864 --> 00:08:52,531
AND IT WAS ME WHO WOULD LEARN

222
00:08:52,573 --> 00:08:55,369
THAT IT WAS ME THAT WAS
THE BEST YOU'D EVER HAD

223
00:08:55,410 --> 00:08:56,828
I'D BE GOING LIKE THIS.

224
00:09:06,921 --> 00:09:08,131
Ross:
ALL RIGHT, EMILY

225
00:09:08,173 --> 00:09:09,924
AS MUCH AS I LOVE YOU

226
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:13,887
I'M SORRY, I CAN'T MOVE
TO LONDON WITHOUT BEN.

227
00:09:13,928 --> 00:09:16,973
I UNDERSTAND
THAT WOULD BE DIFFICULT.

228
00:09:17,015 --> 00:09:18,808
WOULD YOU PLEASE CONSIDER
MOVING HERE?

229
00:09:18,850 --> 00:09:20,894
I MEAN, YOU WERE GOING
TO MOVE HERE ANYWAY.

230
00:09:20,935 --> 00:09:23,063
Why can't you just do that?

231
00:09:23,104 --> 00:09:25,564
OH, I DON'T KNOW. IT'S JUST...

232
00:09:25,606 --> 00:09:27,650
O-OKAY, OKAY, BUT I KNOW

233
00:09:27,692 --> 00:09:32,406
THAT EVEN THOUGH I'VE BEEN
A COMPLETE IDIOT UP TILL NOW

234
00:09:32,447 --> 00:09:34,574
Y-YOU HAVE TO COME HERE.

235
00:09:34,615 --> 00:09:37,827
You have to, so we can
work this out together.

236
00:09:38,828 --> 00:09:40,247
ALL RIGHT.

237
00:09:40,288 --> 00:09:41,415
A-ALL RIGHT?

238
00:09:41,456 --> 00:09:42,999
DID YOU JUST SAY ALL RIGHT?

239
00:09:43,041 --> 00:09:45,752
I DID. NOW I'M THE IDIOT.

240
00:09:45,793 --> 00:09:48,088
OH, EMILY, THAT IS SO GREAT!

241
00:09:48,129 --> 00:09:49,506
It's going to be so great!

242
00:09:49,548 --> 00:09:53,634
WE'RE GOING TO BE LIKE,
LIKE TWO IDIOTS IN LOVE!

243
00:09:53,676 --> 00:09:55,470
( chuckles )

244
00:09:57,138 --> 00:10:00,141
ROSS, THERE'S ONE THING
THAT REALLY SCARES ME STILL.

245
00:10:00,183 --> 00:10:01,435
YES, TELL ME.

246
00:10:01,476 --> 00:10:02,810
You have to understand

247
00:10:02,852 --> 00:10:05,564
HOW HUMILIATING IT WAS FOR ME
UP ON THAT ALTAR

248
00:10:05,646 --> 00:10:08,275
IN FRONT OF MY ENTIRE FAMILY,
ALL MY FRIENDS.

249
00:10:08,316 --> 00:10:11,445
I KNOW. I AM... I AM SO SORRY.

250
00:10:11,486 --> 00:10:14,613
AND THEN,
AFTER DECIDING TO FORGIVE YOU

251
00:10:14,655 --> 00:10:19,077
SEEING YOU AT THE AIRPORT,
CATCHING OUR PLANE WITH HER.

252
00:10:19,119 --> 00:10:22,163
AGAIN, VERY SORRY.

253
00:10:23,748 --> 00:10:26,585
I MEAN, I CAN'T BE
IN THE SAME ROOM WITH HER.

254
00:10:26,626 --> 00:10:28,962
IT DRIVES ME MAD
JUST THINKING OF YOU

255
00:10:29,003 --> 00:10:30,922
BEING IN THE SAME ROOM AS HER.

256
00:10:30,964 --> 00:10:35,385
EMILY, THERE IS NOTHING
BETWEEN RACHEL AND ME.

257
00:10:35,427 --> 00:10:39,680
Okay? I love you.

258
00:10:39,722 --> 00:10:41,933
ALL RIGHT.

259
00:10:41,975 --> 00:10:45,937
I'LL COME TO NEW YORK,
AND WE'LL TRY TO MAKE THIS WORK.

260
00:10:45,979 --> 00:10:47,564
AH, THAT IS SO GREAT! THAT'S...

261
00:10:47,606 --> 00:10:51,401
AS LONG AS YOU DON'T SEE RACHEL
ANYMORE.

262
00:10:58,658 --> 00:10:59,867
...SO I ASKED EMILY

263
00:10:59,909 --> 00:11:01,661
IF SHE WOULD
COME TO NEW YORK

264
00:11:01,702 --> 00:11:03,830
AND SHE SAID YES.

265
00:11:03,871 --> 00:11:05,081
YES!

266
00:11:05,123 --> 00:11:06,416
NO, NO, NO.

267
00:11:06,458 --> 00:11:10,629
ONLY IF I PROMISED
NEVER TO SEE RACHEL AGAIN.

268
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:12,297
WHAT? YOU CAN'T...

269
00:11:12,339 --> 00:11:13,548
WHAT DID YOU TELL HER?

270
00:11:13,590 --> 00:11:15,800
I TOLD HER I'D HAVE
TO THINK ABOUT IT.

271
00:11:15,842 --> 00:11:18,345
I MEAN, HOW THE HELL
AM I SUPPOSED TO MAKE

272
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:20,180
THIS KIND OF
A DECISION?

273
00:11:20,221 --> 00:11:22,641
I'M ACTUALLY ASKING YOU.

274
00:11:24,142 --> 00:11:26,060
WELL, YOU CAN'T
JUST NOT SEE RACHEL ANYMORE.

275
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:27,395
SHE'S ONE
OF YOUR BEST FRIENDS.

276
00:11:27,437 --> 00:11:29,105
YEAH, BUT HE

277
00:11:29,147 --> 00:11:30,982
CANNOT NOT SEE EMILY.
THAT'S HIS WIFE.

278
00:11:31,024 --> 00:11:32,400
YEAH. RIGHT ON.
THAT'S TRUE.

279
00:11:32,442 --> 00:11:34,319
YEAH, BUT

280
00:11:34,361 --> 00:11:36,446
YOU'VE KNOWN RACHEL
SINCE HIGH SCHOOL

281
00:11:36,488 --> 00:11:39,073
AND YOU CANNOT JUST CUT
HER OUT OF YOUR LIFE.

282
00:11:39,115 --> 00:11:40,659
NO, YOU CANNOT.
THAT'S TRUE.

283
00:11:40,699 --> 00:11:41,909
THANKS FOR THE HELP.

284
00:11:41,951 --> 00:11:43,620
PROBLEM SOLVED.

285
00:11:45,288 --> 00:11:47,207
( phone ringing )

286
00:11:48,375 --> 00:11:49,334
HELLO.

287
00:11:49,376 --> 00:11:50,335
HEY, MON.

288
00:11:50,377 --> 00:11:51,419
Oh, hey, Joe.

289
00:11:51,461 --> 00:11:53,463
WHEN ARE YOU GOING
TO BE ON TV?

290
00:11:53,505 --> 00:11:56,924
SEE, THERE WAS KIND OF A MIX-UP
IN MY AGENT'S OFFICE

291
00:11:56,966 --> 00:12:00,637
BUT I'M STILL ON TV
AND THAT'S GOOD EXPOSURE.

292
00:12:00,679 --> 00:12:02,430
Monica:
YOU'RE NOT ON TV.

293
00:12:02,472 --> 00:12:04,015
UH, OKAY.

294
00:12:04,057 --> 00:12:07,935
HOW... HOW ABOUT NOW?

295
00:12:07,977 --> 00:12:10,313
OH...

296
00:12:10,355 --> 00:12:12,065
YEAH! THERE HE IS!

297
00:12:12,106 --> 00:12:14,942
Hello, New York.

298
00:12:14,984 --> 00:12:18,154
Maybe you just like want
to put the whole duck in there.

299
00:12:18,196 --> 00:12:19,447
Who cares? You know?

300
00:12:19,489 --> 00:12:20,699
Now, I got the legs...

301
00:12:20,739 --> 00:12:22,116
OH! OH!

302
00:12:23,826 --> 00:12:26,996
HOW MANY TIMES
HAVE I TOLD YOU GUYS

303
00:12:27,038 --> 00:12:30,166
TO NEVER WATCH
THE COOKING CHANNEL.

304
00:12:30,208 --> 00:12:31,876
HI, CHANDLER.

305
00:12:31,918 --> 00:12:33,294
HEY.

306
00:12:33,336 --> 00:12:34,379
I NEED THAT BROILING PAN

307
00:12:34,421 --> 00:12:35,714
THAT JOEY BORROWED
THE OTHER DAY.

308
00:12:35,754 --> 00:12:36,797
OH, THAT WAS YOURS?

309
00:12:36,839 --> 00:12:38,466
MM-HMM.

310
00:12:38,508 --> 00:12:42,262
YEAH, WE USED IT WHEN THE DUCK
WAS THROWING UP CATERPILLARS.

311
00:12:42,303 --> 00:12:45,432
WILLIAMS-SONOMA,
FALL CATALOG, PAGE 27.

312
00:12:45,473 --> 00:12:47,225
EXPECT IT IN FOUR TO SIX WEEKS.

313
00:12:48,393 --> 00:12:50,353
UM, HEY, UH,
JOEY'S GOING TO BE

314
00:12:50,395 --> 00:12:53,147
AT THE TELETHON
FOR THE REST OF THE DAY, AND...

315
00:12:53,189 --> 00:12:55,650
WE HAVE THE WHOLE PLACE
TO OURSELVES.

316
00:12:55,692 --> 00:12:57,277
YEAH? SO?

317
00:12:57,318 --> 00:13:01,072
WELL, I JUST THOUGHT MAYBE
YOU'D WANT TO BOOK SOME TIME

318
00:13:01,114 --> 00:13:03,157
WITH THE BEST YOU'VE EVER HAD.

319
00:13:03,199 --> 00:13:05,285
YOU KNOW WHAT, CHAMP?

320
00:13:05,326 --> 00:13:07,036
I THINK I'LL PASS.

321
00:13:07,078 --> 00:13:08,329
WHY?

322
00:13:08,371 --> 00:13:09,497
WHY?

323
00:13:22,594 --> 00:13:24,011
WHAT'S YOUR POINT?

324
00:13:27,932 --> 00:13:31,519
PBS TELETHON.

325
00:13:31,561 --> 00:13:34,105
HEY, JOEY, I JUST WANTED
TO LET YOU KNOW

326
00:13:34,147 --> 00:13:36,274
THAT I FOUND
A SELFLESS GOOD DEED.

327
00:13:36,316 --> 00:13:39,444
I WENT DOWN TO THE PARK
AND I LET A BEE STING ME.

328
00:13:39,486 --> 00:13:42,447
WHAT? WHAT GOOD IS THAT GOING
TO DO ANYBODY?

329
00:13:42,489 --> 00:13:44,031
WELL, IT HELPS THE BEE

330
00:13:44,073 --> 00:13:46,743
LOOK TOUGH
IN FRONT OF HIS BEE FRIENDS.

331
00:13:46,785 --> 00:13:49,704
THE BEE IS HAPPY,
AND I AM DEFINITELY NOT.

332
00:13:49,746 --> 00:13:53,583
YOU KNOW THE BEE PROBABLY DIED
AFTER HE STUNG YOU.

333
00:13:57,545 --> 00:13:59,255
DAMN IT.

334
00:14:02,383 --> 00:14:04,051
BACK ON IN 30 SECONDS, PEOPLE.

335
00:14:10,809 --> 00:14:12,101
HEY, EXCUSE ME.

336
00:14:12,143 --> 00:14:14,729
WOULD YOU MIND SWITCHING
WITH ME? I'M JUST...

337
00:14:14,771 --> 00:14:16,731
OH, NO WAY. I'M
IN THE SHOT, MAN.

338
00:14:16,773 --> 00:14:18,941
COME ON, MAN, YOU'VE
BEEN HERE ALL DAY.

339
00:14:18,983 --> 00:14:20,652
MAN, I'M TAKING
PLEDGES HERE, HUH?

340
00:14:20,694 --> 00:14:21,653
AND WE'RE ON

341
00:14:21,695 --> 00:14:23,404
IN THREE, TWO...

342
00:14:23,446 --> 00:14:25,406
WELCOME BACK
TO OUR FALL TELETHON.

343
00:14:25,448 --> 00:14:27,200
NOW, IF YOU'VE BEEN ENJOYING

344
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:29,327
THE PERFORMANCE
OF CIRQUE DE SOLEIL

345
00:14:29,369 --> 00:14:32,580
AND YOU'D LIKE TO SEE MORE
OF THE SAME KIND OF PROGRAMMING

346
00:14:32,622 --> 00:14:34,040
IT'S VERY SIMPLE.

347
00:14:34,081 --> 00:14:36,459
ALL YOU HAVE TO DO
IS CALL IN YOUR PLEDGE

348
00:14:36,501 --> 00:14:38,586
AND AT THAT TIME
TELL THE OPERATOR--

349
00:14:38,628 --> 00:14:40,046
ONE OF OUR VOLUNTEERS--

350
00:14:40,087 --> 00:14:42,215
WHAT TYPE OF PROGRAMMING
YOU FEEL...

351
00:14:43,966 --> 00:14:45,802
OKAY, THAT'S IT.

352
00:14:45,844 --> 00:14:48,262
I CANNOT MAKE
THIS DECISION.

353
00:14:48,304 --> 00:14:50,223
IT IS TOO DIFFICULT.

354
00:14:50,264 --> 00:14:51,599
I'M JUST GOING
TO LEAVE IT

355
00:14:51,641 --> 00:14:53,267
ENTIRELY UP
TO THE GODS OF FATE.

356
00:14:53,309 --> 00:14:55,603
( rattling )

357
00:14:55,645 --> 00:14:57,271
A MAGIC EIGHT BALL?

358
00:14:57,313 --> 00:14:58,523
YOU CAN'T BE SERIOUS.

359
00:14:58,565 --> 00:15:00,274
YOU CAN'T MAKE THIS
DECISION WITH A TOY.

360
00:15:00,316 --> 00:15:02,485
OH, IT'S NOT A TOY.

361
00:15:03,778 --> 00:15:06,447
WELL, I DON'T KNOW
WHAT ELSE TO DO.

362
00:15:06,489 --> 00:15:08,115
I MEAN, I EITHER
KEEP MY WIFE

363
00:15:08,157 --> 00:15:10,951
AND LOSE ONE OF MY...
MY BEST FRIENDS

364
00:15:10,993 --> 00:15:13,204
OR I KEEP MY FRIEND
AND GET DIVORCED

365
00:15:13,246 --> 00:15:15,373
FOR THE SECOND TIME
BEFORE I'M 30.

366
00:15:15,415 --> 00:15:18,459
SO IF ANYONE ELSE HAS...
HAS A BETTER SUGGESTION

367
00:15:18,501 --> 00:15:21,128
LET'S HEAR IT,
BECAUSE I-I-I GOT NOTHING.

368
00:15:21,170 --> 00:15:22,255
DON'T BE SHY.

369
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:23,673
ANY SUGGESTION WILL DO.

370
00:15:28,678 --> 00:15:30,346
OKAY, THEN.

371
00:15:32,014 --> 00:15:34,975
HERE WE GO.

372
00:15:35,017 --> 00:15:37,978
MAGIC EIGHT BALL--

373
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:41,482
SHOULD I NEVER
SEE RACHEL AGAIN?

374
00:15:44,527 --> 00:15:46,404
"ASK AGAIN LATER."

375
00:15:46,446 --> 00:15:48,573
LATER

376
00:15:48,615 --> 00:15:51,242
IS NOT GOOD ENOUGH.

377
00:15:57,123 --> 00:15:58,583
"ASK AGAIN LATER."

378
00:15:58,625 --> 00:15:59,709
WHAT THE HELL!

379
00:15:59,751 --> 00:16:00,877
THIS IS BROKEN!

380
00:16:00,919 --> 00:16:02,295
THE GAME IS BROKEN!

381
00:16:02,336 --> 00:16:04,589
ALL RIGHT,
LET ME SEE.

382
00:16:06,132 --> 00:16:08,217
WILL CHANDLER HAVE SEX TONIGHT?

383
00:16:09,719 --> 00:16:11,011
"DON'T COUNT ON IT."

384
00:16:14,223 --> 00:16:16,935
SEEMS LIKE IT WORKS
TO ME.

385
00:16:19,646 --> 00:16:21,439
PBS TELETHON.

386
00:16:23,107 --> 00:16:24,484
HEY, PHEEBS.

387
00:16:24,525 --> 00:16:26,193
I WOULD LIKE
TO MAKE A PLEDGE.

388
00:16:26,235 --> 00:16:28,446
I WOULD LIKE TO DONATE $200.

389
00:16:28,488 --> 00:16:30,030
$200? YOU SURE, PHEEBS?

390
00:16:30,072 --> 00:16:32,909
I MEAN, AFTER WHAT SESAME STREET
DID TO YOU?

391
00:16:32,951 --> 00:16:34,535
OH, I'M STILL MAD AT THEM

392
00:16:34,577 --> 00:16:37,455
BUT I ALSO KNOW THAT THEY
BRING HAPPINESS TO LOTS OF KIDS

393
00:16:37,497 --> 00:16:39,290
WHOSE MOMS
DIDN'T KILL THEMSELVES.

394
00:16:39,332 --> 00:16:40,959
YOU KNOW,
SO BY SUPPORTING THEM

395
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:45,755
I'M DOING A GOOD THING,
BUT I'M NOT HAPPY ABOUT IT.

396
00:16:45,797 --> 00:16:48,883
SO, THERE, A SELFLESS GOOD DEED.

397
00:16:48,925 --> 00:16:51,761
AND YOU DON'T FEEL A LITTLE GOOD
ABOUT DONATING THE MONEY?

398
00:16:51,803 --> 00:16:53,012
NO. IT SUCKS.

399
00:16:53,053 --> 00:16:55,932
I WAS SAVING UP
TO BUY A HAMSTER.

400
00:16:55,974 --> 00:16:57,016
A HAMSTER?

401
00:16:57,057 --> 00:16:58,768
THOSE THINGS
ARE LIKE TEN BUCKS.

402
00:16:58,810 --> 00:17:01,270
YEAH, NOT THE ONES
I HAD MY EYE ON.

403
00:17:01,312 --> 00:17:02,772
It looks like

404
00:17:02,814 --> 00:17:05,483
we have surpassed
last year's pledge total.

405
00:17:05,525 --> 00:17:06,943
Thank you, viewers!

406
00:17:06,985 --> 00:17:08,820
And the pledge that did it

407
00:17:08,862 --> 00:17:13,449
was taken by one
of our volunteers... Oh, boy

408
00:17:13,491 --> 00:17:19,163
and may I say, one of our
sharpest-dressed volunteers--

409
00:17:19,205 --> 00:17:21,457
Mr. Joseph Tribbiani.

410
00:17:21,499 --> 00:17:22,500
OH, LOOK!

411
00:17:22,542 --> 00:17:23,877
LOOK! JOEY'S ON TV.

412
00:17:23,918 --> 00:17:25,795
ISN'T THAT GREAT?

413
00:17:25,837 --> 00:17:28,464
HEY, MY PLEDGE GOT JOEY ON TV.

414
00:17:28,506 --> 00:17:31,676
OH, THAT MAKES ME FEEL SO...
OH, NO!

415
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:40,894
LOOK, MAYBE I GOT
CARRIED AWAY BEFORE

416
00:17:40,935 --> 00:17:43,813
BUT THERE'S SOMETHING
YOU GOT TO KNOW.

417
00:17:43,855 --> 00:17:45,147
IF I'M THE BEST

418
00:17:45,189 --> 00:17:48,526
IT'S ONLY BECAUSE
YOU MADE ME THE BEST.

419
00:17:49,986 --> 00:17:52,446
KEEP TALKING.

420
00:17:52,488 --> 00:17:55,324
I MEAN, I WAS NOTHING
BEFORE YOU.

421
00:17:55,366 --> 00:17:57,869
CALL THE OTHER GIRLS AND ASK.

422
00:17:57,911 --> 00:18:00,162
WHICH WOULDN'T TAKE LONG.

423
00:18:00,204 --> 00:18:03,750
BUT WHEN I'M WITH YOU,
AND WE'RE TOGETHER

424
00:18:03,791 --> 00:18:07,086
OH... MY... GOD.

425
00:18:11,674 --> 00:18:12,926
REALLY?

426
00:18:12,967 --> 00:18:16,095
OH... OH... MY... GOD.

427
00:18:18,056 --> 00:18:19,933
WELL, I UNDERSTAND
IF YOU NEVER WANT

428
00:18:19,974 --> 00:18:23,561
TO SLEEP WITH ME AGAIN,
BUT THAT WOULD BE WRONG.

429
00:18:23,603 --> 00:18:27,023
WE'RE TOO GOOD.

430
00:18:27,065 --> 00:18:31,235
WE OWE IT TO SEX.

431
00:18:31,277 --> 00:18:33,237
WELL, IF WE OWE IT...

432
00:18:34,822 --> 00:18:35,865
OH!

433
00:18:35,907 --> 00:18:38,076
OH, MY!

434
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:39,660
( giggling )

435
00:18:39,702 --> 00:18:41,120
WHEN IS JOEY GOING
TO BE HOME?

436
00:18:41,161 --> 00:18:42,496
WELL, I WAS
KIND OF HOPING

437
00:18:42,538 --> 00:18:44,040
WE COULD DO THIS
WITHOUT HIM.

438
00:18:44,082 --> 00:18:45,374
HMM, YEAH.

439
00:18:45,416 --> 00:18:46,834
OH, NO, NO, NO, NO.

440
00:18:46,876 --> 00:18:48,461
LEAVE THE GLOVES ON.

441
00:18:48,502 --> 00:18:50,379
BUT I JUST CLEANED
THE BATHROOM.

442
00:18:50,421 --> 00:18:52,506
YEAH, WHY DON'T
WE LOSE THE GLOVES.

443
00:18:52,548 --> 00:18:53,507
YEAH.

444
00:18:53,549 --> 00:18:54,801
OKAY.

445
00:18:54,842 --> 00:18:56,552
OKAY. ALL RIGHT.

446
00:18:56,594 --> 00:18:58,429
LET'S SHOW THEM
HOW IT'S DONE.

447
00:18:58,471 --> 00:18:59,430
OKAY.

448
00:18:59,472 --> 00:19:00,723
OW!

449
00:19:00,765 --> 00:19:04,060
YOU KNOW THAT
WASN'T PART OF IT?

450
00:19:04,102 --> 00:19:05,061
I KNOW.

451
00:19:05,103 --> 00:19:06,104
ALL RIGHT.

452
00:19:12,443 --> 00:19:14,779
( knocking )

453
00:19:19,117 --> 00:19:21,077
HI. YOU READY?

454
00:19:21,119 --> 00:19:22,620
WE'RE GOING
TO BE LATE.

455
00:19:22,662 --> 00:19:23,871
FOR WHAT?

456
00:19:23,913 --> 00:19:26,165
FOR STELLA, REMEMBER?

457
00:19:26,206 --> 00:19:29,669
SHE'S GETTING HER GROOVE
BACK IN, LIKE, 20 MINUTES.

458
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:33,255
YEAH, I, UH, TOTALLY FORGOT
ABOUT THAT.

459
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:35,299
DO YOU MIND IF I
TAKE A RAIN CHECK?

460
00:19:35,341 --> 00:19:37,217
I'M WAITING FOR
A CALL FROM EMILY.

461
00:19:37,259 --> 00:19:40,763
WELL... SURE,
I GUESS.

462
00:19:40,805 --> 00:19:44,851
HEY, I HEAR YOU DON'T HAVE
TO GO LONDON. YAY.

463
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:46,477
IT'S NOT THAT EASY.

464
00:19:46,519 --> 00:19:50,606
THERE'S STILL A LOT OF, UH...
RELATIONSHIP STUFF.

465
00:19:50,648 --> 00:19:52,191
LIKE WHAT?

466
00:19:52,232 --> 00:19:53,609
JUST STUFF.

467
00:19:53,651 --> 00:19:58,405
YOU KNOW, UH,
KIND OF WHAT EMILY WANTS.

468
00:19:58,447 --> 00:20:00,533
WELL, WHY DON'T YOU
TALK TO ME ABOUT IT.

469
00:20:00,574 --> 00:20:02,284
MAYBE I CAN HELP.

470
00:20:02,326 --> 00:20:04,411
NO. NO, YOU...
YOU CAN'T HELP.

471
00:20:05,496 --> 00:20:06,998
I MEAN...

472
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:10,584
I KIND OF HAVE TO DO THIS
WITHOUT YOUR HELP.

473
00:20:10,626 --> 00:20:11,794
WELL, I...

474
00:20:11,836 --> 00:20:15,214
I KNOW YOU CAN DO THAT, TOO.

475
00:20:15,255 --> 00:20:20,344
I'M JUST SAYING, IF YOU NEED
SOMEBODY TO TALK TO... HI.

476
00:20:20,386 --> 00:20:22,513
THANKS.

477
00:20:24,264 --> 00:20:25,683
ROSS?

478
00:20:27,351 --> 00:20:30,938
LOOK, WHATEVER THIS RELATIONSHIP
STUFF IS THAT EMILY WANTS

479
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:32,314
JUST GIVE IT TO HER.

480
00:20:32,356 --> 00:20:34,901
COME ON, THE BOTTOM LINE
IS THAT YOU LOVE HER.

481
00:20:34,942 --> 00:20:37,486
SO JUST FIX
WHATEVER SHE WANTS FIXED.

482
00:20:37,528 --> 00:20:38,529
JUST DO IT.

483
00:20:38,571 --> 00:20:39,697
( phone ringing )

484
00:20:39,739 --> 00:20:42,742
I MEAN, YOU'RE GOING
TO HAVE TO TRY.

485
00:20:42,783 --> 00:20:44,077
( ringing )

486
00:20:44,118 --> 00:20:45,578
